message: "If you use or discuss this evaluation artifact, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Goodhart's Game 2.0: A two-track stress test of evaluation-question and governance-repair integrity"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Young
    given-names: Josh
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-16
url: "https://github.com/uberbestest/goodharts-game-2"
repository-code: "https://github.com/uberbestest/goodharts-game-2"
abstract: >-
  An operator-mediated black-box case study testing whether an AI evaluation
  question and a proposed governance repair preserve their intended objective
  under optimization pressure. The record includes a public transcript,
  derived structural audit, bounded categorical verdicts, and an explicit
  claim boundary. The repair track stopped after hard-gate failures rather
  than promoting a proxy-substituting repair.
keywords:
  - AI evaluation
  - Goodhart's law
  - proxy substitution
  - governance
  - black-box auditing
  - evaluation integrity
